commit 0c191515cd980de8e2506f57ff5317c4745c20ed
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Aug 13 21:06:55 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 13 21:06:55 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): SOL-R3-02 — attestation receipts read the committed row, not assembly state
    
    append_attested/append_tick_attested return the signature read back INSIDE
    the write transaction, after the INSERT (any AFTER triggers have fired),
    before commit — one SELECT per write. Restores the construction-grade
    honesty the simplify pass (item 11) regressed; the cached ticks-PRAGMA
    half of item 11 stands. Ceremony paths get the same read-back pre-log,
    pre-commit: a genesis/edit row rewritten out from under its assembled
    signature refuses (UnsignableGenesis/UnsignableEdit, rollback) — a
    receipt that must claim signed cannot honestly report a nulled row.
    No trigger-schema rejection (detection at an ambient boundary).
    
    Mutation regression: trigger-bearing stores yield attestation matching
    fact_signature/tick_signature_state read-back, signed and nulled cases.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfGCNdAoSqKQ34mKevuF

