Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 13 21:11:53 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): SOL-R3-04 — serialize corrupt-index discard/rebuild across concurrent openers
    
    Recovery runs under an interprocess lock FILE beside the index (flock on
    its own fd — also serializes threads; sqlite cannot provide the lock, its
    file is the casualty). Losers re-check under the lock by reopening at the
    path (re-checks corruption AND binds the winner's inode); only a
    still-corrupt index is quarantined — atomic rename to
    <name>.corrupt.<pid>-<seq> (no wall clock), never a blind unlink. The
    locked/no-log re-raise guards stay in front.
    
    Regression: sol's synchronized two-thread harness shape — both openers
    converge on ONE inode, no divergent reads.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfGCNdAoSqKQ34mKevuF

