    fix(engine): SOL-R3-05 — transient sqlite BUSY/LOCKED is 'refused', not failed recovery
    
    RECOVER_THEN_OPEN distinguished BUSY/LOCKED (sqlite_errorcode 5/6, message
    fallback) before the generic sqlite3.Error branch: a held write lock is a
    try-again-later 'refused' with a busy-specific reason — never 'unreadable'
    claiming rebuild-from-log failed when no rebuild ran and the log reads
    fine. Closed status vocabulary holds. The index-not-discarded property was
    already guarded at the store's own open (locked re-raise); this fix is
    preflight's reporting honesty.
    
    Regression: BEGIN IMMEDIATE-held behind index -> refused-busy, index
    inode intact, no quarantine, log untouched.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfGCNdAoSqKQ34mKevuF

