   347	
   348	    The read path's resolution seam. ``resolve_store_path`` is pure — it can
   349	    only *name* the sqlite index — so a fresh clone (log tracked, derived
   350	    index not) resolves to a path that does not exist, and every reader's
   351	    ``if not store_path.exists()`` answers "empty store" for the one
   352	    invocation that should have built it. Resolving through here makes
   353	    materialization part of resolution, so no reader can observe the gap.
